MODULE proof.evidence.lib.

// Kernel-checked proof evidence for theorem contracts, in the vocabulary `bin/zil theorem-audit` reads.
//
// The theorem DSL (libsets/theorem-dsl-ci) states a contract: what a theorem requires and what it guarantees. The
// audit takes a high or critical theorem as proved only with proof evidence it can see: a `proof_token` to a node
// declared `entity:proof`, which it classes as kernel evidence. LEAN_PROOF says that a Lean theorem, checked by the
// Lean kernel, is that evidence. The theorem name is the Lean name with its namespace (Library.Orders.step_bounded).
MACRO LEAN_PROOF(theorem, lean_name):
EMIT theorem:{{theorem}}#proof_token@proof:{{lean_name}}.
EMIT proof:{{lean_name}}#kind@entity:proof.
EMIT proof:{{lean_name}}#engine@engine:lean4.
ENDMACRO.

// The same for a lemma a theorem rests on (the theorem DSL's LEMMA and THEOREM_REQUIRES_LEMMA): a component model's own
// theorem that a composition relies on. The audit's kernel check covers every `entity:proof` node, lemmas' included.
MACRO LEAN_LEMMA_PROOF(lemma, lean_name):
EMIT lemma:{{lemma}}#proof_token@proof:{{lean_name}}.
EMIT proof:{{lean_name}}#kind@entity:proof.
EMIT proof:{{lean_name}}#engine@engine:lean4.
ENDMACRO.
